# Header logo: CMS upload vs legacy static PNG

## Audit 2026-09-16 (live selpic.com.au)

### Canonical CMS (Admin → Logo Image Management) — **new logo IS live**

| Field | Value |
|-------|--------|
| `contentItems` id | `header-logo` |
| `isActive` | `true` |
| `mediaUrl` | `…/cms/header-logo/1789215001838-a2wiua96u-logo.webp` |
| Size | **~16.9 KB** WebP, transparent (alpha) |
| `updatedAt` | **2026-09-12T12:10:04Z** (no newer CMS row as of this audit) |

Sticky **Header** + home **footer** brand image use `pickLogoImageItem` → this `mediaUrl` after storefront CMS sync. **Not** the 91 KB static PNG for the visible header mark when CMS is healthy.

### Where static logos still load (tab / OG — not sticky header)

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `app/layout.tsx` `icons.icon` | **One** tab icon: `/favicon.ico` only (rewrite → `/images/logo.webp`) |
| `next.config.js` rewrite | `/favicon.ico` → `/images/logo.webp` |
| `/apple-touch-icon.png` | iOS home-screen icon |
| OG / Twitter `defaultOgImage` | `/images/logo.webp` (share preview; not a homepage document request) |
| `HEADER_LOGO_STATIC_FALLBACKS` | Only if CMS `mediaUrl` empty/fails |

Do **not** list webp + png + shortcut together in `metadata.icons` — Pingdom HAR (2026-09-17) showed 3× webp + 2× png duplicate fetches.

### How to verify (owner)

1. Network tab → filter `header-logo` → should see `…a2wiua96u-logo.webp` (~17 KB).
2. Also expect `/favicon.ico` or `/images/logo.png` (~91 KB) for **tab icon only** — expected until static assets are replaced.
3. If header still shows old mark: check CMS sync (`Use Logo Image` on, `mediaUrl` non-empty), hard refresh, or failed image → fallback to PNG.

### Do

- Treat Admin logo upload as source of truth for **header/footer brand image**.
- If owner wants zero old-PNG requests: replace `public/images/logo.png`, `public/logo.png`, `public/apple-touch-icon.png`, and/or point `layout.tsx` icons at the CMS WebP URL (separate change).

### Do not

- Assume Network “logo.png” means Admin upload failed — check whether it is favicon/OG vs header `img`.
- Blame Perf LCP on header logo (hero video dominates).
